      ],
      "answer": "No. Under the definition in 29 U.S.C. 49a(6), an \"employment service office\" means a local office of a State agency. The statute does not require the local office itself to accept appropriations or exercise designation authority; rather, pursuant to section 49c, the State accepts chapter provisions by State statute to obtain apportioned appropriations, and the Governor designates or authorizes the creation of the State agency.",
      "conclusion": "no"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "q3",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source": "S0",
          "passage": "F008"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "No. The definition of \"State agency\" in 29 U.S.C. 49a(7) expressly contains the exception \"except in section 49l–2 of this title\" and therefore cannot be applied without that stated exception.",
      "conclusion": "no"
    }
  ]
}
